A||N||7||Seanh||Covering Dash in vinyl||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||05-21-2001||12:45 AM||||Anyone done it? How did you do it? Any pictures? I have my dash out, and would like to cover it in gray vinyl, but dont know how to go about it. I would like padding under the cover also. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||05-21-2001||04:26 PM||||This has been covered before. I dont think it can be done without some sewing. There are some pretty complex curves. May be a way to do it in several pieces if you dont mind a seam showing somewhere. Best way is to get one of like Pisa's custom dashes and cover it and put it in over the original.||||reg||1
Z||000002||spideyfoot||05-21-2001||08:36 PM||||Lets see I would grab a spare dash . Youll need a heat source (hair dryer..), spray on contact cement, hot glue, vinyl, good scissors. The trick is to dart the ends the vinyl at edges to have place to grab and pull around the edges. both surfaces will have to be sprayed with the contact cement. When both surfaces are dryish feeling set the vinyl over the dash you will need to put some polls,sticks or something in between so you can line up both surfaces the pull the polls out to mate the surfaces I would leave the complex curves non sprayed at first youll have to stretch the vinyl(hairdryer) and pull around the curves. I use the hot glue to tack the vinyl behind the piece to help stretch. On areas with vents and stuff cut x's above the hole and roll back to backside. Now Ive done the center consoles in mine and they look real good the dash cant be that much harder. Make sure you get some vinyl you can stretch.||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||05-22-2001||09:11 AM||||Well I could explain this but I think spidey musta watched me upholster my console  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||7
Z||000004||spideyfoot||05-22-2001||05:47 PM||||Yea Im gonna fly back over there and learn Fiberglass next. Do you ever use that foam stuff for a buck to lay your glass on? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||05-22-2001||07:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by spideyfoot:<BR><B>Yea Im gonna fly back over there and learn Fiberglass next. Do you ever use that foam stuff for a buck to lay your glass on? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think I know the foam stuff you are talking about. We used to use it for fibreglass reinforced insulation (cooling).<P>Any other fibreglass projects I usually shape out of craftwood and car body filler, paint it and polish it to a glass like finish. Then take a mould off it, and only then. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||05-22-2001||09:53 PM||||I don't know where he learned it, Aus, but his console looked great all padded and covered... May talk him into doing one for me one of these days... that is, after I get my Aussie body kit installed!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
